<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa's JSE changes small, mid-cap indices.</title>
<headline>S.Africa's JSE changes small, mid-cap indices.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Johannesburg Stock Exchange on Tuesday detailed further amendments to some of its key indices following a bi-annual revision.</p>
<p>It said the changes will be effective from the close of business on June 20.</p>
<p>New inclusions in the mid capitalisation index were Kloof, Amcoal, M&amp;R Hold, Freegold, Adcock &quot;N&quot; shares, Metlife, Mutual &amp; Federal, Cadswep, Servgro, Shoprite, Consol, Avgold and ABI.</p>
<p>Now also included in the small capitalisation index are M-Cell, Senchem, Palamin, Hiveld, Suncrush, Delfood, Randfontein and Gensa.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
